{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Girded</b> — it also declares His mighty acts, for thus it is fitting for the perfect mighty one to be." "<b>And the meaning of mighty</b> — \"you are mighty,\" or it lacks a kaf as is the way: \"and he called [a lion]\" — that is, \"like a lion,\" or the kaf may be missing by complete elision, and this is \"your splendor.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {1 "The examples reference elliptical comparative constructions; 'and he called a lion' alludes to biblical phrases where the comparative kaf is understood though not written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:52.009356639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}